.TH SKATE 1 "2025-03-06" "skate" "Skate, a personal key value store."
.SH "نام (NAME)"
skate \- Skate, a personal key value store\&.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBskate\fP [\fIoptions\&.\&.\&.\fP] [\fIargument\&.\&.\&.\fP]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdelete\fP KEY[@DB]
.RS 4
Delete a key with an optional @ db\&.
.RE
.TP
\fBdelete-db\fP [@DB]
.RS 4
Delete a database
.RE
.TP
\fBget\fP KEY[@DB]
.RS 4
Get a value for a key with an optional @ db\&.
.RE
.TP
\fBOPTIONS\fP
.RS 4
\fB--b --show-binary\fP
print binary values
.RE
.TP
\fBhelp\fP [command]
.RS 4
Help about any command
.RE
.TP
\fBlist\fP [@DB]
.RS 4
List key value pairs with an optional @ db\&.
.RE
.TP
\fBOPTIONS\fP
.RS 4
\fB--d --delimiter\fP
delimiter to separate keys and values
.TP
\fB--k --keys-only\fP
only print keys and don't fetch values from the db
.TP
\fB--r --reverse\fP
list in reverse lexicographic order
.TP
\fB--b --show-binary\fP
print binary values
.TP
\fB--v --values-only\fP
only print values
.RE
.TP
\fBlist-dbs\fP
.RS 4
List databases\&.
.RE
.TP
\fBset\fP KEY[@DB] [VALUE]
.RS 4
Set a value for a key with an optional @ db\&. If VALUE is omitted, read value from the standard input\&.
.RE
